{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist","id":1487803,"title":"Why are Vampires so calm with the fact that spirits exist?!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-24T16:47:32-07:00","id":1487803,"title":"Why are Vampires so calm with the fact that spirits exist?!","content":"This is something that has never made much sense to me in lore, you see a Giovanni/Tremere/Blood Magician summon Wraiths/Elemental spirits/Something else entirely out of nowhere, and your first reaction is &quot;meh''?<br /> <br /> In every single clanbook, including the ones about clans with blood magic, they will downplay the abilities of the magic using clans. So you're telling me that no vampire who has heard/seen a Giovanni speak to a wraith isn't freaking out that ghosts actually exist and that there are vampires that can enslave them? Are you telling me that a vampire that has seen a Tremere summon a spirit using Elemental Mastery/Spirit Manipulation, didn't have their whole world view shattered by the fact that there are such things as spirits and that certain vampires can summon them? What about demons? The Red List is public to all Vampires, with three of them being known infernalists. Why are the Kindred in power the only ones worried, why is no one else freaking out over the fact that this is plausible proof that demons exist, and can be summoned, which means that Hell exists?<br /> <br /> The Baali Clanbook goes into detail about the creatures they serve/imprison/enslave, it explores the relationships different factions of the Baali have with these creatures, and how they view these creatures. No other blood magic clan does that with their respective blood magic tradition. The Giovanni whose signature power necromancy, which revolves around wraiths, are never shown pondering if enslaving the souls of the deceased is a bad thing, they never stop for a second and think &quot;Am I going to hell for this?&quot;. What about the Tremere that are knowledgeable about the umbra or know paths/rituals that deal with spirits/umbra? They seriously never stop for a second to ponder where all these spirits came from? These are the same complaints I have about Assamite Sorcerers, Kolduns, Sadhana practitioners, Lector Priests, e.t.c. Seriously, no Lector Priest has ever wondered if demons were actually servants of Set?<br /> <br /> It's crazy that none of the books go into this!<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T16:55:09-07:00","id":1487805,"title":"","content":"Did you know that North Korea could launch an artillery barrage large enough to wipe Seoul off the map (And that's with &quot;conventional&quot; artillery)?<br /> <br /> The people in Seoul do; they've known for decades. Eventually, they became mostly numb to it. <br /> <br /> There's only so much fear the mind can process, for better or for worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T16:55:49-07:00","id":1487806,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the whole setting has downplayed how huge it is that the spirit-world exists, even werewolf. I mean, there is an entire universe of allies available to garou, a universe they can pop in and out of like they were Rick Sanchez. That's insane, yet the setting treats it as almost a minor roleplaying thing, just a chance to emulate stuff like Pocahontas talking to the tree spirit in a Disney movie.<br /> <br /> Access to another dimension is insane, absolutely bonkers, yet Necromancers aren't treated as a big deal, and even werewolves are considered dangerous purely because of their physical abilities, not their absolutely Rick Sanchez bonkers dimension hopping ability.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T17:15:32-07:00","id":1487808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487806#post1487806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the whole setting has downplayed how huge it is that the spirit-world exists, even werewolf. I mean, there is an entire universe of allies available to garou, a universe they can pop in and out of like they were Rick Sanchez. That's insane, yet the setting treats it as almost a minor roleplaying thing, just a chance to emulate stuff like Pocahontas talking to the tree spirit in a Disney movie.<br /> <br /> Access to another dimension is insane, absolutely bonkers, yet Necromancers aren't treated as a big deal, and even werewolves are considered dangerous purely because of their physical abilities, not their absolutely Rick Sanchez bonkers dimension hopping ability.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly! Sect warfare, deadly vampire politics, and even the Antedeuvians are nothing compared to the Umbra and it's inhabitants, yet no one cares!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T17:17:00-07:00","id":1487809,"title":"","content":"Because vampire magic does not invoke Paradox, it means they can show mortals that ghosts and spirits exists. That would probably be enough of a shock to their system that some would probably Awaken just processing the experience that utterly shattered their worldview, so why aren't mages trying to manipulate vampires into doing this ? I can see it being against the Code of Ananda, alongside Akashic and Euthanatoi philosophy. But the Order of Hermes would definitely want to experiment with this, to codify a semi reliable process.<br /> <br /> I agree that living in a world where the veil of the supernatural was parted for them, they are more willing to believe in what they would call myths as mortals and eventually it makes them less shocked by more weirdness. However, ghosts remove the afterlife from an unconfirmed possibility into facts that were documented by blood magic for ages. Spirits not only add a new layer of complexity to all reality, but the Umbra encompasses entire dimensions, with nuances and laws of physics beyond the wildest imagination of sci-fi authors. Its everything science and faith speculated about higher realities, in a blend that sometimes makes the distinction hard to see. You would expect them to at least react like Stephen Strange did when the Ancient One showed him the multiverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T17:21:28-07:00","id":1487811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487806#post1487806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the whole setting has downplayed how huge it is that the spirit-world exists, even werewolf. I mean, there is an entire universe of allies available to garou, a universe they can pop in and out of like they were Rick Sanchez.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really anything like that since Rick never gets stuck on the wall and the other universes are actually other timelines instead of the soul of the world, the accumulated wreckage of everything that has existed, or whatever other concept an otherworld happens to be anchored on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's insane, yet the setting treats it as almost a minor roleplaying thing, just a chance to emulate stuff like Pocahontas talking to the tree spirit in a Disney movie. </div> </div> </div>Vampires can't usually go to the Middle Umbra, so they're going to be incredibly unfamiliar with it and probably just assume that there might be a few strange things that they can't see. Even vampires with Auspex 5+ and a jones for out of body experiences are likely going to be interacting with ghosts an overwhelming majority of the time, and not Naturae or banes. This is going to color their expectations such that they can't see past it. The number of vampires that's seen a Triatic spirit jump out of the gauntlet and had any dots to connect and who didn't die the Final Death from the experiences is also low; such experiences are liable to drive them to drink the blood of someone highly intoxicated in order harvest the necessary copium. It wouldn't help their case that any other vampires would probably be somewhere between &quot;Cool story, bro!&quot; and &quot;Get a load of this lick!&quot;, leading them to doubt their sanity and just write the experience off as a dream.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Access to another dimension is insane, absolutely bonkers, yet Necromancers aren't treated as a big deal, and even werewolves are considered dangerous purely because of their physical abilities, not their absolutely Rick Sanchez bonkers dimension hopping ability. </div> </div> </div>It really, really helps to drop the sci-fi interpretation of the spirit worlds. Of course they're going to sound off, absurd, and absent any grandeur if you keep projecting absurdity onto them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T17:24:48-07:00","id":1487812,"title":"","content":"I'm going to suggest something surprising: I don't think most vampires actually believe what you're talking about if they aren't the kind of person who believed in them to begin with.<br /> <br /> You first have to deal with the paradigm shift that &quot;vampires exist&quot; obviously and that's going to be something that modern secular materialists are already going to be blown away. They might be able to adjust the majority of their worldview by believing vampires are natural predators, some sort of mutant, or otherwise creatures of science. These people are wrong. Vampires are magical and defy all conventional science to the point that you CAN scientifically study them but it would create an entirely new field of study as well as state the majority of what you know about others is wrong.<br /> <br /> Which leads to point two, &quot;magic is real.&quot; If you're a modern secular materialist, you're going to have enough trouble with vampirism but that's going to get into the fact that Tremere (and let's stick with the base Seven Clans to start with) can do something fundamentally DIFFERENT than what other vampires can with superpowers. They can mark a wall with a squiggly line in blood and then you flat out can't enter that place anymore. Plenty of vampires will try to say, &quot;No, no, Blood magic is just Disciplines with a bit more weirdness.&quot;<br /> <br /> But taking a step further, &quot;Spirits are real.&quot; Well, after Point A and Point B, it's probably less of a leap than you might think. Because if you're not a modern secular materialist then you've probably come from a society that already believes in spirits. Plenty of cultures believe in angels, demons, and so on anyway. Many more believe in an afterlife so the idea that both of these exist is something that will probably be less surprising than you might think if you're anyone other than someone who dismissed these things as superstition in life.<br /> <br /> Even then, I'd argue if you ARE a modern secular materialist vampire, you might actually dismiss these things because you know at this point:<br /> <br /> * Mind control exists<br /> * Memory alteration<br /> * Magic that can do weird stuff<br /> * Possibly illusion powers as the Ravnos are as common as the Hecata<br /> * The real life Charlatans<br /> <br /> Assume our modern secular materialist vampire, call him Fred the Brujah, hears that the Hecata are a bunch of mobsters (because the Putenesca is assumed to be the Hecata by 90% of people), that can talk to the dead and control their spirits. Are you going to believe that or that the rumor mill has gotten out of hand or they're a bunch of frauds like everyone else who &quot;talks to ghosts&quot;? (And aren't necessarily frauds in the World of Darkness anyway but are still probably 90% frauds).<br /> <br /> But if you AREN'T Fred, by the time you find out about spirits, you've already been led far down the Rabbit Hole and may come from a culture that already believes in spirits and the supernatural that you might react to the discovery with, &quot;Okay, sure.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am a religious person in RL but if I'm a vampire, I might go, &quot;Oh, Zeus is real too. I believe it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-24-2022, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T17:33:26-07:00","id":1487813,"title":"","content":"Zeus being real might be more horrifying than vampirism, given how he tends to act and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T17:39:15-07:00","id":1487814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487805#post1487805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you know that North Korea could launch an artillery barrage large enough to wipe Seoul off the map (And that's with &quot;conventional&quot; artillery)?<br /> <br /> The people in Seoul do; they've known for decades. Eventually, they became mostly numb to it.<br /> <br /> There's only so much fear the mind can process, for better or for worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>This basically. After you know vampires are real, anything becomes possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T18:06:55-07:00","id":1487818,"title":"","content":"First, I think that simply the fact that they're vampires means they've come to terms that the supernatural is real. If vampires are real, then why not werewolves, wizards, ghosts, spirits, fairies, and all sorts of other things? So I don't think it's as shocking as all that for them. Now a newly turned vampire who has just encountered the supernatural may not know how much of the supernatural legends and stories are true and to what extent, but they'll learn fairly quickly. Their adjustment to this new worldview will have already occurred by the time they are released, and actually encounter other supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> <i>Brock, if pirates really exist that means Santa Claus and the tooth fairy can even be real, right? It's like all bets are off.<br /> Hank, nobody ever said pirates don't exist.<br /> So you agree with me that this is impossible!</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6QOG-9OgPY4\" data-code=\"6QOG-9OgPY4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6QOG-9OgPY4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Second, when it comes to spirits and ghosts, most vampires will actually never encounter one. Or if they do, it's of a limited nature. The Gauntlet and the Shroud do a lot to protect the physical realm from them, and while their charms and powers might be impressive, most of the time what they do can be far easier replicated by other means. I don't think that's a &quot;meh&quot; reaction. It's just the difference between actually being in a warzone, and simply learning that there's a war in a far away country.<br /> <br /> There is also the issue that certain people (characters and players) who want to play down any kind of shock or amazement because they want to portray an attitude of &quot;I've seen this all before, and it doesn't impress me.&quot; That is often a BS reaction done because they don't want to lose face, or think this kind of roleplaying means their character is a badass. It's boring roleplay, but it's unfortunately typical. Just for different reasons.<br /> <br /> Third, I do actually think that those occultist vampires who are conjuring spirits and ghosts actually discuss the issues that you are mentioning. The Tremere should have Hermetic theories on the nature of the cosmos and role of the spirits. Necromancers should have theories on the underworld and nature of ghosts. In terms of actual game play, these are the kind of discussions I do see happen between PCs and NPCs. Those are either good roleplayers, or new players who don't know the lore and want to understand. When PCs don't talk about them, it is generally because 1) they do know the lore OOC and just assume a lot of IC knowledge, or 2) those kind of discussions aren't fun for them and they want to get back to something they do find fun. But those are ultimately OOC issues and not IC issues.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the WoD suffers from a lack of mystery nowadays since so much of its lore is known. When the &quot;real&quot; answer is easily researched by players, it ends the kind of speculation that characters should be doing. This is one reason why I, when I am the ST, like to have NPCs explain things in different ways that don't match the established lore (though it doesn't contradict it either). Don't mention the terms of art of the World of Darkness. It's &quot;another dimension&quot; not the &quot;Umbra&quot;. There are &quot;cracks in reality&quot; not &quot;a low Gauntlet.&quot; The movie Ghostbusters is great with stuff like this.<br /> <br /> <i>Sir, what you had there is what we refer to as a focused, non-terminal, repeating phantasm or a class-five full-roaming vapor.</i><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=suaggiDNKQ0\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=suaggiDNKQ0\" data-code=\"suaggiDNKQ0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/suaggiDNKQ0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I find that when you eschew known game terminology for other descriptions, you are more likely to obtain more interest from your players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T21:46:45-07:00","id":1487844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487812#post1487812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to suggest something surprising: I don't think most vampires actually believe what you're talking about if they aren't the kind of person who believed in them to begin with.<br /> <br /> You first have to deal with the paradigm shift that &quot;vampires exist&quot; obviously and that's going to be something that modern secular materialists are already going to be blown away. They might be able to adjust the majority of their worldview by believing vampires are natural predators, some sort of mutant, or otherwise creatures of science. These people are wrong. Vampires are magical and defy all conventional science to the point that you CAN scientifically study them but it would create an entirely new field of study as well as state the majority of what you know about others is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that when someone is turned into a vampire... and they find out that werewolves also exist, and they find out that magic exists and in fact there's a whole clan of wizard-vampires, it's not a huge buy-in to accepting that maybe something like ghosts can exist too. For sure there will be a few vampires who flatly refuse to entertain the idea that any of those things exist, but I think even the most skeptical will end up saying, &quot;Okay, so werewolves and ghosts and wizards... that's not really what we're dealing with. Just some sort of unexplained phenomenon that lets people turn into wolf-men, lets people's residual thoughts continue to exist after death and some form of blood power that lets people summon up fireballs and conjure up storms. I hear there's a clan of vampires that can turn into snakes, and I saw Gangrel Joe turn himself into a wolf last week. So I guess that stuff could exist too.&quot;<br /> <br /> You're more likely to find these sort of super skeptics among the Anarchs of Caitiff. It's really hard to be skeptical when you're part of the Sabbat or attending Camarilla functions with the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-25-2022, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T21:57:01-07:00","id":1487845,"title":"","content":"That's the rub, isn't it? Once you become a Vampire, you have to wonder what ISN'T real, what monsters DON'T exist. <br /> <br /> How is John Q Vampire going to know the difference between a Ghost or a Spirit? What makes a Mummy different than a Lich? And heaven help the poor sod if he laughs at the wrong Changeling...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T23:49:58-07:00","id":1487848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487805#post1487805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you know that North Korea could launch an artillery barrage large enough to wipe Seoul off the map (And that's with &quot;conventional&quot; artillery)?<br /> <br /> The people in Seoul do; they've known for decades. Eventually, they became mostly numb to it.<br /> <br /> There's only so much fear the mind can process, for better or for worse.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487845#post1487845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the rub, isn't it? Once you become a Vampire, you have to wonder what ISN'T real, what monsters DON'T exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fully agree. Plus, the contrast between awakened and unawakened people in the WoD is artificially amplified to help the suspension of disbelieve. Once someone crosses over into the realm of the supernatural, they get hit by the full impact of what it entails. As sleepers, the setting has most of them deny such things are even possible- despite plenty of breaches of the Masquerade, Veil etc.<br /> <br /> I never played CtD, but I really like the concept of Autumn People and have adapted it for other splats (swapping Banality for True Faith in VtM, as kind of anti-Marauders in MtA, or quasi-Drones in WtA). They are a great way to emphasize the contrast between the banal perception of the mortal world and the zoo of supers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T02:23:36-07:00","id":1487851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487845#post1487845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the rub, isn't it? Once you become a Vampire, you have to wonder what ISN'T real, what monsters DON'T exist.<br /> <br /> How is John Q Vampire going to know the difference between a Ghost or a Spirit? What makes a Mummy different than a Lich? And heaven help the poor sod if he laughs at the wrong Changeling...</div> </div> </div> </div>Brujah: &quot;I mean, yeah, why NOT aliens.&quot;<br /> <br /> Irish Tremere: &quot;Changelings aren't aliens.&quot;<br /> <br /> Brujah: &quot;What are they?&quot;<br /> <br /> Irish Tremere: &quot;Extra-dimensional child abducting psychic entities.&quot;<br /> <br /> Brujah: &quot;Aliens.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T03:24:13-07:00","id":1487856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487851#post1487851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Brujah: &quot;I mean, yeah, why NOT aliens.&quot;<br /> <br /> Irish Tremere: &quot;Changelings aren't aliens.&quot;<br /> <br /> Brujah: &quot;What are they?&quot;<br /> <br /> Irish Tremere: &quot;Extra-dimensional child abducting psychic entities.&quot;<br /> <br /> Brujah: &quot;Aliens.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aliens are defined as individuals who come from a foreign nation or country. So you aren't exactly wrong. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T03:52:17-07:00","id":1487858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487856#post1487856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Aliens are defined as individuals who come from a foreign nation or country. So you aren't exactly wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the original BOOK OF THE WYRM, one of the Pentex executives believes he's helping aliens conquer the world and the other Board members make fun of him for it.<br /> <br /> I'm like, &quot;Because<i> that's </i>a dumb interpretation of what's going on.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-25-2022, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T06:48:34-07:00","id":1487879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist#post1487803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something that has never made much sense to me in lore, you see a Giovanni/Tremere/Blood Magician summon Wraiths/Elemental spirits/Something else entirely out of nowhere, and your first reaction is &quot;meh''?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is... you don't. All of these are pretty damn rare, and Tremere as a principle prefer to keep the other Kindred in the dark about what they can or cannot do as it allows them to play the mysterious know it alls even when they're bullshitting you in the face. Most Vampires alive will never encounter a Giovanni. So it comes down to legends and hearsay, and even for those magic users you do encounter doesn't mean that they have all the skills in the book.<br /> <br /> In general, the splats do not have the understanding of the world, culture and mysteries that we as readers of the books do. They live in insular societies with little interaction between different cities, letalone with the strange and weird elements of the setting.<br /> <br /> Another thing to think about is, is it relevant to what Vampire is and what it's about? Because, it's not. Vampire is about politics, degeneration, humanity, lack thereof and finding amusement in a world that tries to fuck with you while you hope to be immortal. Even when it is about the mysteries of the universe, it's about the mysteries relevant to the Vampires - which means it's all about them and their curse and their horrible horrible progenitors and/or uncaring God.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T07:00:29-07:00","id":1487882,"title":"","content":"It helps the World of Darkness is also turtles all the way down. If you ARE a scientist or occultist who has his entire paradigm shaken, they can spend the next few centuries studying the supernatural to discover the truth.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> And they will be even more confused.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T07:49:04-07:00","id":1487887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487812#post1487812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to suggest something surprising: I don't think most vampires actually believe what you're talking about if they aren't the kind of person who believed in them to begin with.<br /> <br /> You first have to deal with the paradigm shift that &amp;quot;vampires exist&amp;quot; obviously and that's going to be something that modern secular materialists are already going to be blown away. They might be able to adjust the majority of their worldview by believing vampires are natural predators, some sort of mutant, or otherwise creatures of science. These people are wrong. Vampires are magical and defy all conventional science to the point that you CAN scientifically study them but it would create an entirely new field of study as well as state the majority of what you know about others is wrong.<br /> <br /> Which leads to point two, &amp;quot;magic is real.&amp;quot; If you're a modern secular materialist, you're going to have enough trouble with vampirism but that's going to get into the fact that Tremere (and let's stick with the base Seven Clans to start with) can do something fundamentally DIFFERENT than what other vampires can with superpowers. They can mark a wall with a squiggly line in blood and then you flat out can't enter that place anymore. Plenty of vampires will try to say, &amp;quot;No, no, Blood magic is just Disciplines with a bit more weirdness.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> But taking a step further, &amp;quot;Spirits are real.&amp;quot; Well, after Point A and Point B, it's probably less of a leap than you might think. Because if you're not a modern secular materialist then you've probably come from a society that already believes in spirits. Plenty of cultures believe in angels, demons, and so on anyway. Many more believe in an afterlife so the idea that both of these exist is something that will probably be less surprising than you might think if you're anyone other than someone who dismissed these things as superstition in life.<br /> <br /> Even then, I'd argue if you ARE a modern secular materialist vampire, you might actually dismiss these things because you know at this point:<br /> <br /> * Mind control exists<br /> * Memory alteration<br /> * Magic that can do weird stuff<br /> * Possibly illusion powers as the Ravnos are as common as the Hecata<br /> * The real life Charlatans<br /> <br /> Assume our modern secular materialist vampire, call him Fred the Brujah, hears that the Hecata are a bunch of mobsters (because the Putenesca is assumed to be the Hecata by 90% of people), that can talk to the dead and control their spirits. Are you going to believe that or that the rumor mill has gotten out of hand or they're a bunch of frauds like everyone else who &amp;quot;talks to ghosts&amp;quot;? (And aren't necessarily frauds in the World of Darkness anyway but are still probably 90% frauds).<br /> <br /> But if you AREN'T Fred, by the time you find out about spirits, you've already been led far down the Rabbit Hole and may come from a culture that already believes in spirits and the supernatural that you might react to the discovery with, &amp;quot;Okay, sure.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I am a religious person in RL but if I'm a vampire, I might go, &amp;quot;Oh, Zeus is real too. I believe it.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I must confess, vampirism would blow my mind away. After that, I dont know if I would be more or less prone to abandon my materialism afterwards. Maybe any kind of weird after would just be &quot;well, whatever. Unicorns you say? Yeah, ok&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T08:02:11-07:00","id":1487888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487851#post1487851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Brujah: &amp;quot;I mean, yeah, why NOT aliens.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Irish Tremere: &amp;quot;Changelings aren't aliens.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Brujah: &amp;quot;What are they?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Irish Tremere: &amp;quot;Extra-dimensional child abducting psychic entities.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Brujah: &amp;quot;Aliens.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The technical term would be &quot;Ultraterrestrials&quot;; that's aliens from another dimension, as opposed to &quot;extraterrestrials&quot;, who are aliens from other planets","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T09:37:21-07:00","id":1487895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487879#post1487879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing to think about is, is it relevant to what Vampire is and what it's about? Because, it's not. Vampire is about politics, degeneration, humanity, lack thereof and finding amusement in a world that tries to fuck with you while you hope to be immortal. Even when it is about the mysteries of the universe, it's about the mysteries relevant to the Vampires - which means it's all about them and their curse and their horrible horrible progenitors and/or uncaring God.</div> </div> </div> </div>This all gets thrown out the window when you have paths like spirit manipulation/elemental mastery/necromancy. Freaking Path of Karma revolves around controlling and picking your reincarnation, how is this not a major plot point within the metaplot!<br /> <br /> If I was a neonate, ancillae, or even elder who just saw some vampire summon a spirit, politics, and angsting over my humanity is the last thing I'm going to do. So what if it isnt relevant to my lifestyle? Im cancelling all my meetings and getting to bottom of what that thing actually was. The fact that elemental spirits exist, also puts a lot of doubt on the claim that vampires are danmed. Can you magine what would happen if vampires realized that there were alternate dimension that were filled with many creatures that were formed purely from human thought? Everyone would freak out! Noddists would be panicking, none of the lore they dug up talks at all about this. The sects themselves are going to be thrown into dissaray. The fact that theres multiple alternate dimensions is downright maddening! Especially for vampires not used to such sci-fi/high fantasy tropes (probably used that wrong).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-25-2022, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T09:51:53-07:00","id":1487898,"title":"","content":"You seem to be labouring under the interpretation that these things are commonly known even among the masters of the occult. They are not. Most Tremere will only ever know the Path of Blood. It's exotic to have Movement of the Mind and Path of Flames. Everything else is beyond esoterica.<br /> <br /> Stop assuming the people in the setting read the books you are reading or that all these overinflated Paths are actually practiced by a significant number of people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:16:45-07:00","id":1487904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487898#post1487898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be labouring under the interpretation that these things are commonly known even among the masters of the occult. They are not. Most Tremere will only ever know the Path of Blood. It's exotic to have Movement of the Mind and Path of Flames. Everything else is beyond esoterica.<br /> <br /> Stop assuming the people in the setting read the books you are reading or that all these overinflated Paths are actually practiced by a significant number of people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know that, but what about those who know of the Giovanni's necromancy? Practically everyone knows the Giovanni are necromancers. And surely some have heard of tremere doing stuff like summoning spirtis, which should be passed around in some conversations. Plus, theres old skool sorcery that foucuses on interacting with spirits, from what I read it seems that this school is pretty well known throughout the Anarchs. To lesser extent theres the punk and new age schools as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 02-10-2023, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T10:56:06-07:00","id":1487915,"title":"","content":"But how many of them <i>do</i> know a Giovanni (later Hecata)?<br /> <br /> Whether they're in Venice or in Boston, the Clan is repeatedly mentioned to <i>keep</i> to <i>themselves</i>. It's not like they're running around town, calling up ghosts and raising up zombies, with Dead Man's Party blasting from speakers. They're hiding in mansions or penthouse apartments, surrounded by muscle. You're not going to see a Giovanni unless they want you to.<br /> <br /> A conclusion I've come to attempting to write about vampires (even my ill fated Twilight parody) is that they're a lot like the mob. They officially &quot;don't exist,&quot; anyone who knows they DO exist is either about to be &quot;taken care of&quot; or &quot;given an offer they can't refuse,&quot; and (a lot of them) seem to have a lot of money lying around. In addition to all of that, the Giovanni are literally <i>portrayed</i> as waking straight off the set of the Godfather, so they're all that and then some. <br /> <br /> Giovanni should be almost as secretive as the Tzimisce. Ergo, Vampires outside the Clan are not likely to see a bunch of shuffling zombies or hear wailing spirits. If they're lucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T11:11:15-07:00","id":1487919,"title":"","content":"It's also important to note that the Giovanni were supposed to be a very small clan. Their original clan description explicitly stated that they only embraced three vampires in every generation. If you hold that &quot;a generation&quot; means every thirty years, that is only one a decade. The Giovanni should only have whatever numbers they had at the time of the Promise of 1528 plus fifty more. In their original conception, there's probably only around a hundred Giovanni total in the entire world. Of course, that got thrown out the window once their first clanbook came out because Justin Achilli is incapable of keeping to any canon that might counter his own pet ideas. That meant the Giovanni suddenly became a lot larger than intended. There's a lot to like in that original clanbook, but it badly needed a strong editor who kept him to the actual concept and force him to rewrite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T13:12:14-07:00","id":1487930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487904#post1487904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I know that, but what about those who know of the Giovanni's necromancy? Practically everyone knows the Giovanni are necromancers. And surely some have heard of tremere doing stuff like summoning spirtis, which should be passed around in some conversations. Plus, theres old skool sorcery that foucuses on interacting with spirits, from what I read it seems that this school is pretty well known throughout the Anarchs. To lesser extent theres the ounk and new age schools as well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'm going to make an argument that I don't think that most vampires know what a Giovanni is.<br /> <br /> I think you need an Occult score of one to know there's 13 Clans.<br /> <br /> One of the things the books emphasized more earlier but never really got away from is the average Neonate generally knows:<br /> <br /> * The main Seven Clans but there's probably more. In V5 they'll know about Lasombra, the Ministry [NOT Setites], and Banu Haqim, albeit in the broadest terms.<br /> * There's Disciplines<br /> * Anarchs<br /> * Camarilla<br /> * A Prince<br /> * Don't tell anyone about vampires or we will fuck you up/kill you.<br /> * The Elders get pissy about other things like feeding in their favorite spot<br /> * Maybe some vampires will mention Caine like they're speaking about Jesus or the End of the World<br /> <br /> Everything else has to be learned in-game or bought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-25-2022, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T14:40:52-07:00","id":1487942,"title":"","content":"I agree with Asmodai and CTPhipps. When it comes to the World of Darkness, we must assume Ignorance is <i>the default</i>.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is a realm of hundreds of concurrent and competing conspiracies. Even conspiracies within conspiracies. All of whom have a vested interest in maintaining a tight lid on any and all information. The conspiracies keep information secret even from each other, because information is not only dangerous, it's <i>currency</i>. <br /> <br /> When I imagine what your &quot;average&quot; vampire knows - most of which will be Neonates, simply due to attrition - I look at how Vampire's setting was presented in 1st edition. A Neonate doesn't even necessarily know who's in charge in a city, let alone the political situation both within their sect and outside of it.<br /> <br /> Vampire politics in many ways is a dance of pretending you're stronger than you are, pretending you know more than you do, and looking for ways to learn even basic things about other vampires. If you're lucky, you've got a Mentor willing to pass down knowledge because they like you or because you're useful. But even Mentors won't necessarily reveal all to their students/Childer. Either because they want to keep a grip on them, because they fear this information being used against them, or because there are gaps in their knowledge and don't want to tip their hand about it.<br /> <br /> As for matters of spirits, a vast, VAST majority of vampires will never encounter one. At least, they may go centuries before they have the opportunity. (Not surprising, since a majority of all vampires won't reach Ancillae age, regardless of sect). Most spirits that do interact with vampire politics (if not directly with vampires themselves) do so from a position of anonymity. Most don't have the power to manifest visually or in auditory in the physical world, and those that do may not want to (manifesting is not free, nor always necessary). If a vampire's unlife was touched by the presence of a spirit, they're unlikely to know it happened. Or else it involved some weirdness the vampire couldn't explain.<br /> <br /> Those vampires who truck with spirits are few and far between. Giovanni are reclusive, and Tremere users of Spirit Manipulation are similarly rare. Nor are they likely to &quot;summon&quot; a spirit where other vampires can see it, save in the most dire circumstances (&quot;summoning&quot; a spirit isn't free). Most vampires with the Paths or Rituals needed to do any spirit stuff don't have the skill necessary to &quot;summon&quot; anyway. When a spirit is used by a vampire, it's likely to be indistinguishable from regular blood magic to the lay vampire.<br /> <br /> We know, from the books, that Tremere will occasionally make big displays of arcane might. Usually a complicated and time-consuming Ritual, triggered to go off at a time and circumstance to give the illusion it was a spontaneous working. Because, yes, Clan Tremere must periodically make themselves seem stronger than they really are. But Clan Tremere also benefits from keeping their full capabilities a secret. Remaining mysterious, so everyone both respects their power and comes begging for Boons.<br /> <br /> This can create the impression, among ignorant vampires, that Tremere can either do basically anything, or are charlatans. A secular materialist vampire doesn't need to think Tremere are &quot;doing magic&quot;. They can be lulled into thinking they have some weird vampire power - as all vampires do - that they dress up in mysticism to bilk superstitious Elders from the Dark Ages. (The secular materialist is wrong, of course, but characters are allowed to be wrong.)<br /> <br /> My point is that while a vampire could, due to being a vampire, open themselves up to accepting other supernatural things, this doesn't mean they will be forced to do so by circumstance. Keeping others in the dark as to what is real is a standard tactic of the World of Darkness conspiracies. The World of Darkness is a large, dense place. A vampire could spend centuries studying, and never learn half of what exists printed in our sourcebooks. Let alone encounter them personally. Accepting that ghosts or spirits <i>might</i> exist, and encountering one, are two different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T16:54:17-07:00","id":1487949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1487895#post1487895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was a neonate, ancillae, or even elder who just saw some vampire summon a spirit, politics, and angsting over my humanity is the last thing I'm going to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're a walking corpse that by all means should be stiff and rotting in a coffin. You lack vital signs and has been like that for years. You do not age, and can have a realistic expectation of living unabated and unchanged for centuries to come. Your internal organs are shriveled beyond the ability to even pretend basic functions, yet they process blood as if you were fully alive, even delivering the effects of drugs your dead body can't actually metabolize in any way. From the blood taken you're able to call forth mystic powers that already can't be explained by any school of thought known to humankind.<br /> <br /> Are you that surprised that ghosts and spirits, the things about 60% of the world population already believes to be real, are real?<br /> <br /> Even if a given character witness some blatant proof of the existence of such entities, their surprise isn't likely to last. Maybe politics would be the last thing you would worry about for some time, but with enough time you would just get used to such things. Even a completely normal human would, as do the many normal humans that can swear to their gods that they witnessed such phenomena irl and do so frequently. Imagine a creature that is A) Immortal, B) supernatural itself and C) dependent on politics for survival.<br /> <br /> Unless you're under the impression that somehow everything else in a vampire's nightly life is perfectly mundane, there's plenty of hints of terrible forces behind the world in the basic assumptions that vampires exist and wield Disciplines. Spirits are probably the simplest explanation already for a lot of people. And as far as most vampires can tell, spirits existing don't change a thing, as if they exist, they always existed and that changed nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T17:14:16-07:00","id":1487950,"title":"","content":"Mind you, I do think vampires are going to be the supernaturals most likely to dismiss the existence of other supernaturals even if they have proof. They're people who have the power of perception alteration, mind-control, illusion, memory-alteration,and the ability to gas light just about anyone into believing anything since the entire point of their existence is to maintain the fiction they don't exist.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;Sure, Tony, you saw a Hecata summon your great uncle from the dead and you talked to him for hours. Don't be stupid. I know they like to claim they can speak with the dead and other bullshit but don't you think we'd be overwhelmed with ghosts if they existed? You and I have killed like fifty people between us. It's all mind-games and Disciplines with these people. You can't trust anything you see or hear and have to go with your gut. Which is that we're the only things out here. What's next? Gods? Terminators? Frigging fairies? Please.&quot;</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T18:10:42-07:00","id":1488234,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of someone coming to say to you in an Elysium or something, on your third month as a vamp. &quot;Hey, fairies exist dude&quot;<br /> You just would look at them funny like &quot;just what the fuck is that supposed to mean? what do you mean by 'fairies'?&quot;<br /> <br /> Same goes for ghosts. Are they invisible people haunting stuff?<br /> Are werewolves furries by moonlight, forgetful people by day?<br /> Are all mummies made of toilet paper locked in coffins?<br /> Are spirits generic terms for anything?<br /> Can you prove any of this? <br /> <br /> But I really agree that WoD lacks mystery sometimes. As well as we need to take the default as ignorant in all WoD things but the basics for your own in-setting survival.<br /> But hell, the game about mysticism, sorcery and occult powers (Mage) can be a sunday morning cartoon or Marvel movie sometimes.<br /> Cthulhu and Kupala aren't frightening forces of unknown nature if you know there is people manipulating and bossing around spirits, having teas with demons and making crazy magics in thee afterlife. Tremere's really shouldn't have been part of the 7 pillar Clans, even if most don't know what their magics are capable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T11:23:43-07:00","id":1488371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488234#post1488234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are werewolves furries by moonlight, forgetful people by day?</div> </div> </div> </div>That one's a bit closer to home for most vampires, and the practical answer is &quot;terror of lingering mortality made flesh&quot;, or &quot;why you don't go into the woods&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T18:15:14-07:00","id":1488515,"title":"","content":"Most of the Cosmology of WoD means there is probably a heaven, but there is definitely a hell and in some cases many hells. Yet every splat in WoD insists on ignoring those facts. You would think that having Demons being a playable splat would make the Sabbat reconsider their value of human life or ethical behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T19:58:25-07:00","id":1488524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488515#post1488515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the Cosmology of WoD means there is probably a heaven, but there is definitely a hell and in some cases many hells. Yet every splat in WoD insists on ignoring those facts. You would think that having Demons being a playable splat would make the Sabbat reconsider their value of human life or ethical behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a playable splat, Demons come from a place that, while can be called <i>Hell</i>, can't receive human souls. Human souls cannot be found on most of the many spirit realms, and the few where they <i>can</i> simply do not account for more than a fraction of all people dying.<br /> <br /> While it is true that the setting has Hells and whatnot, it also goes to great lengths to make the final destiny or definitive nature of human souls just as mysterious as it is irl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T20:14:07-07:00","id":1488526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488524#post1488524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a playable splat, Demons come from a place that, while can be called <i>Hell</i>, can't receive human souls. Human souls cannot be found on most of the many spirit realms, and the few where they <i>can</i> simply do not account for more than a fraction of all people dying.<br /> <br /> While it is true that the setting has Hells and whatnot, it also goes to great lengths to make the final destiny or definitive nature of human souls just as mysterious as it is irl.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think a sabbath would be able to know from where those &quot;demons&quot; come from, be they Fallen, Wyrm spirits or whatever. They would just call it all &quot;demon&quot; and be left to wander what would be of their immortal souls should they die...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T20:44:32-07:00","id":1488528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488515#post1488515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the Cosmology of WoD means there is probably a heaven, but there is definitely a hell and in some cases many hells. Yet every splat in WoD insists on ignoring those facts. You would think that having Demons being a playable splat would make the Sabbat reconsider their value of human life or ethical behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons are delusional. And one can point towards the Underworld to demonstrate that heaven and hell don't exist - even with the 1000 Hells, those are just places cobbled together by powerful spirits using pieces of the high and low Umbra. And many members of the Sword of Caine consider themselves damned by Caine's curse anyway, or performing God's will on earth by being terrible monsters, so it's not really an issue for them. <br /> <br /> That said though, the issue of hell is a pretty big part of any Wan Kuei's story, so not every splat in the WoD insists on ignoring it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T22:32:51-07:00","id":1488534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488526#post1488526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont think a sabbath would be able to know from where those &quot;demons&quot; come from,</div> </div> </div> </div>Which just makes the cosmology even more pointless as a &quot;proof&quot; of something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T23:33:54-07:00","id":1488538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488524#post1488524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a playable splat, Demons come from a place that, while can be called <i>Hell</i>, can't receive human souls. Human souls cannot be found on most of the many spirit realms, and the few where they <i>can</i> simply do not account for more than a fraction of all people dying.<br /> <br /> While it is true that the setting has Hells and whatnot, it also goes to great lengths to make the final destiny or definitive nature of human souls just as mysterious as it is irl.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a no with a yes.<br /> <br /> Demons come from the Abyss, which cannot house human souls.<br /> <br /> However, the Abyss is at the center of the Labyrinth which is part of the only place human souls are known to go (The Underworld).<br /> <br /> Which is akin to saying human souls cannot be found in Chicago but they only exist in Illionois.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/memb