/strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488528#post1488528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demons are delusional. And one can point towards the Underworld to demonstrate that heaven and hell don't exist - even with the 1000 Hells, those are just places cobbled together by powerful spirits using pieces of the high and low Umbra. And many members of the Sword of Caine consider themselves damned by Caine's curse anyway, or performing God's will on earth by being terrible monsters, so it's not really an issue for them. <br /> <br /> That said though, the issue of hell is a pretty big part of any Wan Kuei's story, so not every splat in the WoD insists on ignoring it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of knowledge would not be know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T03:51:04-07:00","id":1488551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488550#post1488550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That kind of knowledge would not be know</div> </div> </div> </div>I also feel this is something that the World of Darkness deliberately offers contradictory evidence on. The Demons of the Fallen believe in a Judeao-Christian world (albeit a very blasphemous one) to directly contrast the Werewolf cosmology.<br /> <br /> If you're a mage or a changeling, you can flat out go to Heaven and talk to your dead aunt and uncle....because you believe you can.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T10:03:03-07:00","id":1488577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488538#post1488538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons come from the Abyss, which cannot house human souls.<br /> <br /> However, the Abyss is at the center of the Labyrinth which is part of the only place human souls are known to go (The Underworld).<br /> <br /> Which is akin to saying human souls cannot be found in Chicago but they only exist in Illionois.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a no with a yes.<br /> <br /> We have four places called Abyss in the cosmology, and no evidence to any of them being the same or even linked. So while it is true that maybe the Fallen come from the center of the Labyrinth, that's not a canonical truth, just a possibility raised by readers.<br /> <br /> Also, the rest of what I said still applies: the Labyrinth does not account for more than a fraction of the souls of the dead around the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T10:05:42-07:00","id":1488579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488577#post1488577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually a no with a yes.<br /> <br /> We have four places called Abyss in the cosmology, and no evidence to any of them being the same or even linked. So while it is true that maybe the Fallen come from the center of the Labyrinth, that's not a canonical truth, just a possibility raised by readers.<br /> <br /> Also, the rest of what I said still applies: the Labyrinth does not account for more than a fraction of the souls of the dead around the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>One would certainly hope not everyone goes to Hell.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T11:40:58-07:00","id":1488588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488528#post1488528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demons are delusional. And one can point towards the Underworld to demonstrate that heaven and hell don't exist - even with the 1000 Hells, those are just places cobbled together by powerful spirits using pieces of the high and low Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Middle and Low. There's not much Astral in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T15:29:23-07:00","id":1488605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488551#post1488551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also feel this is something that the World of Darkness deliberately offers contradictory evidence on. The Demons of the Fallen believe in a Judeao-Christian world (albeit a very blasphemous one) to directly contrast the Werewolf cosmology.<br /> <br /> If you're a mage or a changeling, you can flat out go to Heaven and talk to your dead aunt and uncle....because you believe you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's what Im saying. WE, the unkown Gods that play with the lives of the innocent creatures of the WoD for our amusement, we know that a Mage can go to the spirit world of dreams where the Chorist will find a bunch of winged humanoids singing songs to the glory of the lord because that's the creation of the <u>Mage's mind</u>.<br /> <br /> The poor critters of the WoD have no way of knowing any better thou.<br /> <br /> I mean, &quot;Avatars&quot; are &quot;shards of the One&quot;, sure thing, we know that - but the Chavrakanti do NOT.<br /> <br /> We play this world from a position of a &quot;omniscient narrator&quot;. The people (or creatures) living in the WoD do not.<br /> <br /> If a vampire sees an &quot;angel&quot;, who's in fact just an Umbrood spirit, he has no way of knowing any better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T15:33:47-07:00","id":1488609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488579#post1488579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One would certainly hope not everyone goes to Hell.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the WoD is just a Cthulh-esque universe created to torture the poor creature living in it.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Wyrm, the Baali, the Nafandi and the Specters are actually right, and the best course of action is to obliterate this cursed existance and surrender to niilism.<br /> <br /> Maybe all the hope in this world is just an illusion created to increase even more the overall suffering.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the ones living in such an insidious prison nightmare wouldnt know any better regardless","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T16:38:47-07:00","id":1488616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488551#post1488551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're a mage or a changeling, you can flat out go to Heaven and talk to your dead aunt and uncle....because you believe you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually not true. That's not exactly how Mage works and not how Changeling works at all.<br /> <br /> For Mage, while your beliefs shape a lot of things, it can't make and populate a new Realm in the Umbra out of your wishes. Mages explore the Umbra to look for those things, and they know human souls aren't going <b>in bulk</b> anywhere they can reach. You may reach realms that match your superficial image of Heaven, but won't hind your dead relatives there unless those are spirits fooling you, that's a different thing from your beliefs coming true and Mages know the distinction, they're Will-Workers, not Imbeciles.<br /> <br /> Changelings... have nothing to do with belief. Imagination, yes, not belief. And the Dream does not give you whatever you want. If there is a place that seems like Heaven, Changelings will still know it is just a piece of the Dreaming, fleeting as they all are, and inhabitants are dream entities, something they're relatively able to distinguish and most of the time are Chimera. But you can't go there just 'cause you believe or want to, and dead souls have no reason to go there any more than they have to go anywhere on the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Added, Changelings do not know where fae souls go upon death if it's not going to reincarnate for some reason. They're not meant to die in the first place, but when they do, their destiny is anyone's guess. The Sidhe have a legend for their own souls that involve traveling to a strange, grey space that's not in the Dreaming, and may be in the Dark Umbra, but it is a confuse legend and don't cover deaths by Cold Iron as far as anyone can tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488605#post1488605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WE, the unkown Gods that play with the lives of the innocent creatures of the WoD for our amusement, we know that a Mage can go to the spirit world of dreams where the Chorist will find a bunch of winged humanoids singing songs to the glory of the lord because that's the creation of the <u>Mage's mind</u>.<br /> <br /> The poor critters of the WoD have no way of knowing any better thou.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's the key point.<br /> <br /> OoC the setting has too many blanks and inconsistencies for us to give a definitive answer about anything. IC it gets infinitely worse, as the characters do not have our view of the whole. They have fragmented access to fragmented information whose sources they can and should question. In the end, it is really hard that any particular character will have access to information that breaks their worldview even more than becoming supernatural and being introduced to their own society already did. And even if they do, this info will always come in such a limited, biased way that they can interpret the bigger picture however they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T20:46:18-07:00","id":1488653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488550#post1488550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That kind of knowledge would not be know</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on which splat and were. When it comes to the Wan Kuei, the Emerald Courts the Hsien and other denizens in Asia, the history of the Yama Kings and of Yomi aren't a secret or anything. I imagine anyone with 1 dot of occult would have the basic understanding of the history of the Spirit Kingdom and the 1000 Hells. <br /> <br /> Among western splats it's interesting to note that while there's an Underworld, you can't go to Heaven or Hell. Those aren't places you can travel to, whether travelling through the Umbra or the Underworld. I expect most Giovanni and other vampires who deal extensively with the Underworld don't actually believe that Heaven or Hell really exist since they communicate with the dead on a fairly regular basis and those guys don't seem to know if Heaven or Hell exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T21:30:46-07:00","id":1488658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488653#post1488653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on which splat and were. When it comes to the Wan Kuei, the Emerald Courts the Hsien and other denizens in Asia, the history of the Yama Kings and of Yomi aren't a secret or anything. I imagine anyone with 1 dot of occult would have the basic understanding of the history of the Spirit Kingdom and the 1000 Hells. <br /> <br /> Among western splats it's interesting to note that while there's an Underworld, you can't go to Heaven or Hell. Those aren't places you can travel to, whether travelling through the Umbra or the Underworld. I expect most Giovanni and other vampires who deal extensively with the Underworld don't actually believe that Heaven or Hell really exist since they communicate with the dead on a fairly regular basis and those guys don't seem to know if Heaven or Hell exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Giovanni would also know that most of the dead do NOT go to the Underworld. So, they must be going somewhere.<br /> <br /> And, whatever type of knowledge any single one splat knows, that will always be an incomplete knowledge. What is the Yomi worlds after all? The Wan Kuei surely will have their dogmatic ideas which they believe to be the utter higher truths of the universe, however, they are wrong.<br /> <br /> Even the Fallen (demons) are probably wrong on most of their assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T21:54:47-07:00","id":1488662,"title":"","content":"The point is that for some splats, Heaven and/or Hell absolutely exist. Whether those are objective truths or not, they're accepted as truths by those splats. Every Wan Kuei was once in Yomi and managed to escape. And for them, the denizens of Hell pose an existential threat to the world, so combating Hell is a major part of their storyline. The history of the Yama Kings and of Yomi is fairly common knowledge among them (is that history objective fact or is everything a lie? For the Wan Kuei it's the truth). For Werewolves, Heaven and Hell are just human myths, those places don't exist. &quot;Gods&quot; do exist, but they're just high Umbral spirits (and the Christian deity would be dismissed as the Patriarch, an aspect of the Weaver). But the Ancestors spirits of werewolves live in the Umbra and be communicated with, and if a werewolf lives their life correctly they can join them in death. For them, there's no doubt that an afterlife exists. <br /> <br /> For the Giovanni, I would suspect that a common belief is that anyone who dies simply gets sucked into Oblivion at the moment of death. Only ghosts with strong wills or ties to the living are able to resist the pull of Oblivion and continue existence in the Underworld. For them, believing in Heaven or Hell is simply a matter of faith no different from mortals. There's no evidence that either of those places exist and that good souls go to heaven when they die and bad souls go to hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T21:56:08-07:00","id":1488663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488616#post1488616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's the key point.<br /> <br /> OoC the setting has too many blanks and inconsistencies for us to give a definitive answer about anything. IC it gets infinitely worse, as the characters do not have our view of the whole. They have fragmented access to fragmented information whose sources they can and should question. In the end, it is really hard that any particular character will have access to information that breaks their worldview even more than becoming supernatural and being introduced to their own society already did. And even if they do, this info will always come in such a limited, biased way that they can interpret the bigger picture however they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont get it. How does this helps the case of the Sabbath being inhumane?<br /> <br /> Im a skeptical, utterly materialistic atheist who doesnt believe in NOTHING that cant be explained in a naturalistic manner; that means, I dont believe in angels, demons, heaven or hell, I dont believe in souls nor do I believe in other hidden worlds.<br /> <br /> However, if I were turned into a vampire I probably would convert to christianism in the very next day!<br /> <br /> The Critters of the WoD suffer from a severe lack of knowledge and understanding on how the WoD truly works.<br /> <br /> And, due to all these gaps in their knowledge, they would invariably seek support in something that could provide SOME answer; and that's where religion comes into.<br /> <br /> And, most religions in human history did not praise simple slaughter and psychopatic behavior; the &quot;cainite religion&quot;, in particular, has many roots on judaism with all the talk about Caine and such. So I do indeed find it admirable that there arent more vampires that takes abhraamic religions premisses and dogmas more seriously, or even buddhists, hinduists etc etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T22:17:14-07:00","id":1488665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488662#post1488662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that for some splats, Heaven and/or Hell absolutely exist. Whether those are objective truths or not, they're accepted as truths by those splats. Every Wan Kuei was once in Yomi and managed to escape. And for them, the denizens of Hell pose an existential threat to the world, so combating Hell is a major part of their storyline. The history of the Yama Kings and of Yomi is fairly common knowledge among them (is that history objective fact or is everything a lie? For the Wan Kuei it's the truth). For Werewolves, Heaven and Hell are just human myths, those places don't exist. &amp;quot;Gods&amp;quot; do exist, but they're just high Umbral spirits (and the Christian deity would be dismissed as the Patriarch, an aspect of the Weaver). But the Ancestors spirits of werewolves live in the Umbra and be communicated with, and if a werewolf lives their life correctly they can join them in death. For them, there's no doubt that an afterlife exists. <br /> <br /> For the Giovanni, I would suspect that a common belief is that anyone who dies simply gets sucked into Oblivion at the moment of death. Only ghosts with strong wills or ties to the living are able to resist the pull of Oblivion and continue existence in the Underworld. For them, believing in Heaven or Hell is simply a matter of faith no different from mortals. There's no evidence that either of those places exist and that good souls go to heaven when they die and bad souls go to hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cant tell for sure that the Giovanni knows what the Oblivion is, or rather (because we ourselves do not lnow), if they ever heard about Oblivion other than some weird ghost stories.<br /> Besides, the Giovanni heard the same stories about &quot;God&quot; and the &quot;curse of Caine&quot; as everybody else. That does give some credit to at least some distorted view of judaic/christianism worldviews. Not to mention that the Giovanni were born during the middle ages in christian Europe, not some ancient pagan civilization like Rome, Egypt or Babylon.<br /> <br /> Now, I believe there has been some sort of miscommunication. My entire point was agreeing with CTTPhips that maybe the Sabbath should have a better apreciation for human life, since they would probably believe in angels and heaven and fear divine retribution. So yes, I agree with you that each group inside the WoD believes in what they believe, and would act accordingly. And that was my point, that maybe the Sabbath should be a little different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T08:05:16-07:00","id":1488697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488662#post1488662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that for some splats, Heaven and/or Hell absolutely exist. Whether those are objective truths or not, they're accepted as truths by those splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but then the fact those truths aren't objective does mean we're still in the same waters as always: the characters don't <b>know</b> things. They <b>believe</b>. And access to a bit more information didn't made it less of a matter of faith. Which means some characters can defy that faith and true believers aren't objectively more right than anyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488663#post1488663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont get it. How does this helps the case of the Sabbath being inhumane?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that the proposed theory was that they would have objective reason to worry about their actions condemning them to Hell, when there's no such proof and what they have is already faith.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat believes that as vampires they're supposed to be monsters, want it or not. And this is a religious belief more than anything, they're the Church of Caine, with priests and bishops and whatnot. Their whole deal is to be a religious organization, and if some just pay lip service to this, for many others this is for real.<br /> <br /> We can discuss if this belief system makes sense, and I would be one to agree that it doesn't make a lot for me. But their assumption is that their monstrosity already <b>is</b> this religious support. Saying they should abandon their religion because they have proof of religion is a silly thing, as the proof given do not prove any particular religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T09:03:40-07:00","id":1488707,"title":"","content":"As for the Sabbat: it really depends on the Path. The Cathari believe in reincarnation. You're going to be part of the physical world again and again forever, so its best to serve the god of the physical world, since that's the god that rules your fate 99% of the time.<br /> <br /> The Feral Hearters are mostly agnostic about spirituality, and regard the Path more as a method of achieving inner-peace. It's an almost psychiatric path in some respects. To the degree that it is spiritual at all, it's basically saying that apparently god wants you to be a predator, so you'd best go about being the most perfect predator you can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T09:43:58-07:00","id":1488715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488697#post1488697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the sense that the proposed theory was that they would have objective reason to worry about their actions condemning them to Hell, when there's no such proof and what they have is already faith.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat believes that as vampires they're supposed to be monsters, want it or not. And this is a religious belief more than anything, they're the Church of Caine, with priests and bishops and whatnot. Their whole deal is to be a religious organization, and if some just pay lip service to this, for many others this is for real.<br /> <br /> We can discuss if this belief system makes sense, and I would be one to agree that it doesn't make a lot for me. But their assumption is that their monstrosity already <b>is</b> this religious support. Saying they should abandon their religion because they have proof of religion is a silly thing, as the proof given do not prove any particular religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I guess my point was more in the vein of analyzing wether or not their belief system makes a whole lot of sense or not, which in my opinion does not, rather than disputing their <b>subjective</b> truth on the matter.<br /> <br /> But then again, religions form and disappear, and althought it may not make much sense initially, it simply keeps being spread after it's created so, why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T20:13:12-07:00","id":1488756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488707#post1488707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Sabbat: it really depends on the Path. The Cathari believe in reincarnation. You're going to be part of the physical world again and again forever, so its best to serve the god of the physical world, since that's the god that rules your fate 99% of the time.<br /> <br /> The Feral Hearters are mostly agnostic about spirituality, and regard the Path more as a method of achieving inner-peace. It's an almost psychiatric path in some respects. To the degree that it is spiritual at all, it's basically saying that apparently god wants you to be a predator, so you'd best go about being the most perfect predator you can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, but the end result is roughly the same (for the purposes of the argument being made).<br /> <br /> First, you must pay lip service at least to the Church of Caine, even if your actual belief is diverse. Path Followers have to deal with this fact all the time, either by being an interpretation of the Church, something diverse that can still live side by side with the Church, or a &quot;heresy&quot; that must hide itself to avoid persecution within the Church.<br /> <br /> But beyond that and more importantly, for the question at hand (how do you deal with the information you have on the cosmology of the world) you're most of the time just exchanging between religious beliefs from the overall Church of Caine to your Path. Or otherwise using the Path as your system to understand and make assumptions about the facts you know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488715#post1488715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I guess my point was more in the vein of analyzing wether or not their belief system makes a whole lot of sense or not, which in my opinion does not, rather than disputing their <b>subjective</b> truth on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, but that was not what I was arguing about.<br /> <br /> The thread is, in the end, about how do you come to terms with the things you learn about the cosmos beyond the material veil of reality in the WoD. And the proposition was that this knowledge should lead to repentance and humane treatment (to a degree, at least, as we're discussing Sabbat basic ideology).<br /> <br /> So this is the context of my argument: regardless of the validity of their beliefs under <b>other</b> forms of scrutiny, the cosmology itself is no reason to reach such conclusions. It may be a reason to change your initial spirituality, but it doesn't really reinforces any particular faith more than the mundane, material world already does. It adds a lot of variables, but no confidence to any conclusion you draw from them.<br /> <br /> Becoming a vampire can make you convert to a faith, or even to a disbelief in God (as for some it would prove that the world is too broken to be the handwork of a perfect being), but the particular faith would still be as personal a matter as ever. Or at least, defined by other factors, not this particular one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T12:35:02-07:00","id":1488868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488707#post1488707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Sabbat: it really depends on the Path. The Cathari believe in reincarnation. You're going to be part of the physical world again and again forever, so its best to serve the god of the physical world, since that's the god that rules your fate 99% of the time.<br /> <br /> The Feral Hearters are mostly agnostic about spirituality, and regard the Path more as a method of achieving inner-peace. It's an almost psychiatric path in some respects. To the degree that it is spiritual at all, it's basically saying that apparently god wants you to be a predator, so you'd best go about being the most perfect predator you can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since vampires don't always kill their victims and aren't forced to, they're more often just micropredators of blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T19:08:11-07:00","id":1488916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488868#post1488868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since vampires don't always kill their victims and aren't forced to, they're more often just micropredators of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>The perfect predator isn't necessarily the bigger predator (or the bigger consumer among predators).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T19:23:13-07:00","id":1488921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488868#post1488868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since vampires don't always kill their victims and aren't forced to, they're more often just micropredators of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the better classification would be parasites rather than predators. And I believe that fits perfectly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T21:06:20-07:00","id":1488931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488921#post1488921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the better classification would be parasites rather than predators. And I believe that fits perfectly</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> here that <i>micropredator</i> fits them better. While I do know that the distinction between micropredator and parasite is blurry and many consider mosquitoes as parasites, and that vampires are called parasites also as a metaphor due to their relationship with humanity in a Gothic setting being a social parasitism of sorts, at the end of the day I find it just too heavy handed to call them parasites.<br /> <br /> They're micropredators, with an invested interest in not killing their prey. In fact, they do have an invested interest to not have a parasitic relationship at all with their prey, this is just a genre assumption. They're Alpha Predators in the strict sense of not having predators for themselves, except eventual cannibalism.<br /> <br /> And yes, some follow personal philosophies or even Paths that propose their role as feral predators that hunt like savage tigers, but that's just because they're humans at heart, with human ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T14:09:20-07:00","id":1489151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1488931#post1488931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> here that <i>micropredator</i> fits them better. While I do know that the distinction between micropredator and parasite is blurry and many consider mosquitoes as parasites, and that vampires are called parasites also as a metaphor due to their relationship with humanity in a Gothic setting being a social parasitism of sorts, at the end of the day I find it just too heavy handed to call them parasites.<br /> <br /> They're micropredators, with an invested interest in not killing their prey. In fact, they do have an invested interest to not have a parasitic relationship at all with their prey, this is just a genre assumption. They're Alpha Predators in the strict sense of not having predators for themselves, except eventual cannibalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Purrs laughingly in wolf spider Ananasi]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, some follow personal philosophies or even Paths that propose their role as feral predators that hunt like savage tigers, but that's just because they're humans at heart, with human ideas. </div> </div> </div>Then they find out how hard it can be to be a tiger that eats humans and leaves corpses around for other humans to find (setting aside that just about every tiger that eats humans on the reg is typically doing it because some injury prevents them from hunting their typical, likely much more nourishing, prey).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T16:42:49-07:00","id":1489165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist?p=1489151#post1489151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then they find out how hard it can be to be a tiger that eats humans and leaves corpses around for other humans to find (setting aside that just about every tiger that eats humans on the reg is typically doing it because some injury prevents them from hunting their typical, likely much more nourishing, prey).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, don't they live for hundreds of years because the wild stories about them work like the heart of a Setite? Or was it a Lich's philactery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"h